@{
    var portal = ViewData["Portal"] as string ?? "Coach";
}

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-circle-info"></i> Introduction</h2>
    <p>
        In communities with limited recreational opportunities, and parents with limited
        financial resources, it is essential that the school promotes physical education and
        modified junior sport as part of the school curriculum.
    </p>
    <p>
        By removing the obstacles to participation and shifting mind-set, any smooth surface
        can become a safe, caring environment for physical activity within schools and
        communities.
    </p>
    <p>
        This pragmatic approach ensures every learner has access to the benefits of physical
        activity, and helps build a lasting love for recreation, health, and sport.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-bullseye"></i> Vision, Focus &amp; Motto</h2>
    <div class="fia-card-grid">
        <div class="fia-card">
            <h3>Our Vision</h3>
            <p>Promotion of fundamental movement skills through participation in modified
                games during physical education, after school, and holidays.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-card">
            <h3>Our Focus</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Fun</li>
                <li>Enjoyment</li>
                <li>Participation</li>
                <li>Education</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-card">
            <h3>Our Motto</h3>
            <p>"Organise not formalise."</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-circle-question"></i> What &amp; Why</h2>
    <div class="fia-card-grid">
        <div class="fia-card">
            <h3>What is Fun in Action?</h3>
            <p>A programme that promotes FUNdamental Movement Skills and life skills through
                regular participation in modified games. It is age-appropriate and aligned to
                the physical education curriculum in the Foundation and Intermediate Phase.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-card">
            <h3>Why Fun in Action?</h3>
            <p>Aligning with school PE outcomes helps more children attain and enjoy optimum
                health. Success depends on the quality and amount of exposure to fundamental
                movement skills during the normal school day.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-list-check"></i> Key Components</h2>
    <div class="fia-components">
        <div class="fia-component">
            <span class="num">1</span>
            <div class="body">
                <strong>Early Childhood Development</strong>
                <span>Gross motor skills and core muscle development through play.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-component">
            <span class="num">2</span>
            <div class="body">
                <strong>Promotion of Fundamental Movement Skills</strong>
                <span>Aligned with the Life Skills curriculum.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-component">
            <span class="num">3</span>
            <div class="body">
                <strong>Inter-Class Modified Games</strong>
                <span>Increases participation, limited cost to implement, improves learner discipline.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-component">
            <span class="num">4</span>
            <div class="body">
                <strong>Modified Neighbourhood Leagues</strong>
                <span>Cost-effective to implement, increases participation, builds better communities.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-component">
            <span class="num">5</span>
            <div class="body">
                <strong>Junior Modified Club Sport</strong>
                <span>The natural progression from school-level participation into club sport.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-images"></i> Gallery</h2>
    <div class="fia-gallery">
        <div class="fia-gallery-item" onclick="openLightbox(this)">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/athletic_pro_final_transparent.png" alt="Fun in Action gallery photo 1">
        </div>
        <div class="fia-gallery-item" onclick="openLightbox(this)">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/crane_robot_hockey_front_facing.webp" alt="Fun in Action gallery photo 2">
        </div>
        <div class="fia-gallery-item" onclick="openLightbox(this)">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/arctic_fox_robot_hockey.webp" alt="Fun in Action gallery photo 3">
        </div>
        <div class="fia-gallery-item" onclick="openLightbox(this)">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/athletic_pro_final_transparent.png" alt="Fun in Action gallery photo 4">
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-robot"></i> Our Mascot</h2>
    <p>
        The team's early idea was a Duolingo-style animated mascot to make the app feel
        alive for younger players. "Foxy" was the first concept &mdash; but the name
        turned out to already be trademarked, so the team explored a robot direction
        instead, still built around a sporty, friendly feel.
    </p>
    <div class="fia-card-grid">
        <div class="fia-card" style="text-align:center;">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/arctic_fox_robot_hockey.webp" alt="Arctic fox robot concept" style="width:100%;max-width:200px;margin:0 auto 12px auto;display:block;" />
            <h3>Concept: Arctic Fox Robot</h3>
            <p>An early animal-robot hybrid, keeping a nod to the original "Foxy" idea while sitting inside an armoured, robotic body.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-card" style="text-align:center;">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/crane_robot_hockey_front_facing.webp" alt="Crane robot concept" style="width:100%;max-width:200px;margin:0 auto 12px auto;display:block;" />
            <h3>Concept: Crane Robot</h3>
            <p>A tall, bird-inspired build exploring a different silhouette and a sleeker, more mechanical look.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fia-card" style="text-align:center; border-top-color:#1fa3a5;">
            <img src="~/assets/mascots/athletic_pro_final_transparent.png" alt="Final Fun in Action mascot" style="width:100%;max-width:200px;margin:0 auto 12px auto;display:block;" />
            <h3>Final Mascot</h3>
            <p>The friendly, rounded robot design the team settled on &mdash; simple enough to animate, and now used across the app and website.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="fia-section">
    <h2><i class="fa fa-address-card"></i> Contact</h2>
    <div class="fia-contact">
        <div class="row"><i class="fa fa-phone"></i> <span>083 252 6321</span></div>
        <div class="row"><i class="fa fa-envelope"></i> <a href="mailto:funinactionza@gmail.com">funinactionza@gmail.com</a></div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Gallery Lightbox overlay -->
<div id="fia-lightbox" class="fia-lightbox" onclick="closeLightbox(event)">
    <button class="fia-lightbox-close" onclick="closeLightbox(event)" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <img id="fia-lightbox-img" src="" alt="Enlarged gallery photo">
</div>